on and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn5le15ob02re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Asking For and Giving Advice"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the question What should I do? to ask for advice. You can use the modals should and could before the verb to give advice."}, {"type": "example", "content": "What should I do to lose weight?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "You should work it off on your bike. It's good exercise."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You should try to get an autograph from one of the players."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You could try keeping track of the players in this scorebook."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Making and Responding to Requests"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you make and respond to requests, remember to be polite!"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Is there any chance you'd be interested in a baseball game?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Yeah, I would enjoy that."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Would you mind explaining the game to me?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "No problem."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I was wondering if you would want to sit closer to the baseball field."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I don't mind switching seats. Maybe we can catch a foul ball."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Making Requests\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Responding to Requests\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Would you \u2026 ?</br> I'd like to \u2026</br> Would you mind (if) \u2026 ?</br> Would \u2026  be okay?</br> I was wondering if \u2026 </br>Could you \u2026 ?</br> Do you think you could \u2026 ?</br> Is there any chance you could \u2026 ?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Sure, I'll \u2026 </br>Sure, I'd be glad to \u2026</br> No, not at all.</br> Certainly.</br> Yes, of course.</br> I'll see what I can do.</br> I don't mind at all.</br> Of course we can \u2026</br> No problem.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to lose weight"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to decrease your weight with exercise and a good diet"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Sally wants to lose weight after eating a big lunch. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le15ob02aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear on requests and advice."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to work it off"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to do exercise after a big meal"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Sally and Peter work off the big lunch by bike-riding."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le15ob02aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "innovative"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "describes something using new and interesting ideas"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The bike share system around the city is really innovative."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le15ob02aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to take (amount of time)"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the amount of time needed to do something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It takes 30 minutes to get into the city by train."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le15ob02aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "strike"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "when a baseball player misses the ball with his bat"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: That player now has two strikes."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le15ob02aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "pop fly"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "when the baseball is hit high up in the air but not so far"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: When that player hits a pop fly, I hope our team catches it."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le15ob02aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "inning"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "One turn of a baseball game when one team is batting and the other team is catching - this goes until the batting team has 3 players out. Then they switch."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We're now at the 9th inning, so it's our last chance to score."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le15ob02aud07"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Try to write 8 lines explaining the game of baseball."}, {"type": "text", "content": "If you're not sure about the rules, do some research."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Keep it simple, but make your statements clear."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your game instructions with your partner. Ask if they're correct."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I write sports game instructions in English."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I research the game of baseball."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I teach my partner in English how to play baseball."}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"